WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
What leaves a reader stuck on a docs page that looks finished?

2
00:00:04.533 --> 00:00:06.853
Accessibility testing answers that,

3
00:00:06.853 --> 00:00:10.753
because a screen reader follows only the structure in the markup,

4
00:00:10.753 --> 00:00:12.673
not a bold-text heading.

5
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.560
And if only a screenshot shows the request returned 200,

6
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.700
that reader can't confirm success,

7
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.300
so I'd say it in nearby text.

8
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.200
So I'd run a checker on the generated HTML,

9
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.360
then tab through and zoom the page,

10
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.467
because automation can't judge focus or reflow.

11
00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:31.907
Then I'd make that a release gate,

12
00:00:31.907 --> 00:00:36.267
running the checker in the same preview step that checks links and examples.
